; Stage 15 W9 item 13 at a PARAMETER, the position a user hits most. Filed
; against `defstruct`, but the null return is the shared fall-through of
; `parse-type-from-node`, so every caller that reads null as "no annotation"
; carried the same wrong message — param, `let`, `defvar` and return alike.
; Fixing it in one place fixed all of them; this fixture pins that the fix is
; the shared one and not a per-caller patch.
;
; Compiling this must FAIL with:
;   "unknown type: nosuch — not defined anywhere in this compilation unit"
; and specifically NOT with "defn: missing :type on param 'x'".
(defn f (x:(nosuch i32)):i32
  (return 0))

(defn main ():i32
  (return 0))
